CORE
gated_clock_ungated1.sv
--show-rtl
^\$root\.main\.q1\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.d$
^\$root\.main\.q2\[0:0\] register, next-state value: !main\.rst_n \? 1'b0 : main\.d$
^\$root\.main\.q3\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.d$
^\$root\.main\.q4\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.d$
^\$root\.main\.q5\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.d$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Clock gating is only applied when the clock expression depends on
exactly one base clock, when every edge of the event control is gated,
and when the logic consists of and, or, xor, not and the conditional
operator.
